            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a headline, then the Hindi for to be printed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पत्रकार",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पत्रकार — patrakār — \"a journalist\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मीरा पत्रकार बनना चाहती है। Mīrā patrakār bannā cāhtī hai. Mira wants to become a journalist."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine or feminine, by the person meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पत्रकार (patrakār) joins पत्र, a letter or a paper, from Sanskrit pattra, also spelt patra, with -kāra, \"maker, doer\" (Monier-Williams): a modern word for one who makes the papers, a journalist."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
